InternalComponent:
- Should be able to do some kind of function

- Should not be able to take in any parameters, as that will be the job of the abstract internal system types
that will extend it

Chassis:
- Should take in general parameters for the initialization of whatever needs to be initialized, with the class itself providing
an abstract method to allow for initialization using the generalized parameters

- Should be able define an abstract helper method for utility classes that give info on the specs of the chassis, the return type
being an implementation of the ChassisState interface

ChassisState:
- Should be able to define methods for calling certain types from the different chassis's depending on the state type inputted

- Should be able to define methods to also set the state of the chassis's drive modules to ensure that all the information the drive modules
need in order to drive properly will be right there, ready to use

